course: dictionary
lesson: 14290
title: Tricky word: notion
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A notion is an idea or belief, often one that is not fully clear or not quite right. You can have a notion about something without being sure it is true. «I had a notion that school started at nine» means the child thought so, but was not certain.
explain: Context shows which meaning fits. «She took a notion to paint her room purple.» Here a notion is a sudden wish to do something. «He had no notion where he was» means he had no idea at all. Read the words around notion to decide: is it a thought, a wish, or a big idea?
explain: In school, notion can mean a basic idea, like «the notion of fairness». This is a big idea that people think about, not a guess. Ask yourself: is someone guessing, suddenly wanting something, or explaining an important idea?
fact: A notion is an idea or belief, often one that is vague or unsure.
fact: «He had no notion where he was» means he had no idea at all.
fact: «She took a notion to paint her room purple» means she suddenly wanted to do it.
fact: In America, notions can mean small sewing items like buttons, pins and thread.
fact: In maths and science, a notion is a basic idea, like «the notion of a number».
exercise: «I had a notion that school started at nine.» What does notion mean here? | A box of pins and buttons | *An idea or belief that might be wrong | A sudden wish to run away | A fact checked by a teacher
exercise: «She took a notion to paint her room purple.» What does took a notion mean? | Forgot about the paint | *Suddenly decided to do something | Was given a present | Measured the room carefully
exercise: «He had no notion where he was.» What does no notion mean? | He knew the place very well | *He had no idea | He was lost in a shop | He drew a map of the town
test: In America, a shop might sell notions. What are notions there? | *Small sewing items like buttons, pins and thread | Ideas about the future | Old paintings | Sports kit
test: Our teacher talked about «the notion of fairness». What kind of notion is this? | *A basic idea or concept | A silly guess | A sewing item | A sudden wish
exam: Which sentence uses notion to mean a sudden wish? | «Buttons and pins are sold as notions.» | «I had a notion that it would rain.» | *«Ben took a notion to bake a cake at midnight.» | «The notion of infinity is hard to picture.»
